  "design": {
    "decision": "On every trick, choose between following suit and trumping, so trumps go where they win the most; low [♠]s become live winners.",
    "opponent": "Revealed the first time the team trumps while holding the led suit; opponents can no longer count on a long suit running and should lead [♠] to strip trumps.",
    "rationale": "It changes who wins tricks directly and visibly, which the brief asks for. The option-style commons failed because their freedoms rarely mattered, while trumping at will matters on most tricks. The hook is a general card filter on the existing anySuit rule, not per-sigil code.",
    "partners": [
      "e-trump-mult",
      "seed-trump-three",
      "seed-trump-points",
      "cb-become-spade",
      "uc-low-to-spade",
      "uc-low-spade-win"
    ],
    "cluster": "C",
    "draftText": "Your team can play [♠]s even when it can follow suit",
    "hooks": "anySuit gains an optional card filter (`card`). With it, your team may play a matching card from another suit even when it can follow suit, on every trick, or only inside an existing first/last window when one is also given. Leading [♠] before [♠]s are broken stays illegal, and ordinary trump priority applies.",
    "critic": {
      "verdict": "keep",
      "concerns": "Lifting follow-suit for [♠] is a big rule change, and opponents can no longer run long suits, but it is visible once used.",
      "elegance": 4
    }
  },
